# REQUIRES: system-linux
# UNSUPPORTED: msan, asan, hwasan
#
# Within a 3 GB address space, functions whose obligations, or whose specs
# unfolded as deep as their fuel, would take far more end with a verdict
# instead of failing an allocation: what is built is counted as it is built
# and stops at --max-query-nodes. 1200 checks would take about 30 GB.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/many_checks.py 1200 %t/many.cpp
# RUN: ulimit -v 3000000
# RUN: not %cpp-verify --jobs=1 --max-query-nodes=200000 %t/many.cpp -- 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MANY
# RUN: not %cpp-verify --jobs=1 --max-query-nodes=2000000 \
# RUN:   %S/obligation_size_limit.cpp -- -DFUEL 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FUEL

MANY: Unresolved: many_checks [backend=z3] [reason=query.size-limit] (the proof obligations would take at least {{[0-9]+}} expression nodes, more than the limit of 200000 (--max-query-nodes)
FUEL: Verified: small [backend=z3]
FUEL: Unresolved: unfolds [backend=z3] [reason=query.size-limit] (the facts about the specs it applies
